- **Lightweight, dependency-free** (no external libraries)
- Uses **localStorage** for persistence across sessions
- Includes an **in-memory cache** for fast access during a session
- Implements a **time-to-live (TTL)** expiration to keep data fresh
- Handles **race conditions** with a simple lock mechanism
- Limits cache size (e.g., last 3 searched cities) to avoid localStorage bloat
- Uses **timestamps** to expire stale data
- Encodes city names safely for keys (using `encodeURIComponent`)

---

### Recommended Caching Approach

You can combine an in-memory `Map` with localStorage persistence. The in-memory cache speeds up repeated requests during the same session, while localStorage keeps data available across page reloads.

---

### Example Implementation

```javascript
// Cache configuration
const CACHE_KEY = 'weatherAppCache';
const CACHE_TTL = 5 * 60 * 1000; // 5 minutes TTL
const MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES = 3;

// In-memory cache (Map)
const memoryCache = new Map();

// Simple lock flag to prevent race conditions
let cacheLock = false;
const waitForLockRelease = () => new Promise(resolve => {
  const interval = setInterval(() => {
    if (!cacheLock) {
      clearInterval(interval);
      resolve();
    }
  }, 10);
});

// Load cache from localStorage on app start
const loadCacheFromStorage = () => {
  const raw = localStorage.getItem(CACHE_KEY);
  if (!raw) return;

  try {
    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw);
    const now = Date.now();

    // Filter out expired entries
    Object.entries(parsed).forEach(([key, { data, timestamp }]) => {
      if (now - timestamp < CACHE_TTL) {
        memoryCache.set(key, { data, timestamp });
      }
    });
  } catch (e) {
    console.warn('Failed to parse cache from localStorage', e);
  }
};

// Save current memory cache to localStorage
const saveCacheToStorage = () => {
  if (cacheLock) return; // Avoid concurrent writes
  cacheLock = true;

  try {
    // Convert Map to plain object
    const obj = {};
    memoryCache.forEach(({ data, timestamp }, key) => {
      obj[key] = { data, timestamp };
    });

    localStorage.setItem(CACHE_KEY, JSON.stringify(obj));
  } catch (e) {
    console.error('Failed to save cache to localStorage', e);
  } finally {
    cacheLock = false;
  }
};

// Add or update cache entry, evict oldest if over limit
const addToCache = (key, data) => {
  const timestamp = Date.now();

  if (memoryCache.has(key)) {
    memoryCache.delete(key); // Refresh order
  } else if (memoryCache.size >= MAX_CACHE_ENTRIES) {
    // Evict oldest entry (first inserted)
    const oldestKey = memoryCache.keys().next().value;
    memoryCache.delete(oldestKey);
  }

  memoryCache.set(key, { data, timestamp });
  saveCacheToStorage();
};

// Get cached data if valid, else null
const getFromCache = (key) => {
  const cached = memoryCache.get(key);
  if (!cached) return null;

  if (Date.now() - cached.timestamp > CACHE_TTL) {
    memoryCache.delete(key);
    saveCacheToStorage();
    return null;
  }

  return cached.data;
};

// Initialize cache on app load
loadCacheFromStorage();

// Example fetch function with caching
async function fetchWeather(cityName) {
  const key = encodeURIComponent(cityName.toLowerCase());

  // Check cache first
  const cachedData = getFromCache(key);
  if (cachedData) {
    console.log(`Cache hit for ${cityName}`);
    return cachedData;
  }

  // Cache miss: fetch from API
  try {
    const response = await fetch(`https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?q=${encodeURIComponent(cityName)}&units=metric&appid=YOUR_API_KEY`);
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`API error: ${response.status}`);
    }
    const data = await response.json();

    // Add to cache
    addToCache(key, data);

    return data;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Fetch error:', error);
    throw error;
  }
}
```

---

### Explanation

- **Cache key**: Uses URL-encoded lowercase city names to avoid collisions.
- **TTL**: Cached entries expire after 5 minutes to keep data fresh.
- **LRU eviction**: Keeps only the last 3 searched cities in cache, evicting the oldest when adding new entries.
- **Locking**: A simple boolean lock prevents concurrent writes to localStorage.
- **Persistence**: Cache is loaded from localStorage on app start and saved after updates.
- **Error handling**: Fetch errors are thrown to be handled by your UI logic.

